00:19:20,199 --> 00:19:21,325
Does that mean

262
00:19:22,326 --> 00:19:25,246
the shoot will take place
in the States?

263
00:19:25,788 --> 00:19:26,789
Yes.

264
00:19:28,583 --> 00:19:31,794
We begin production in LA
early next year.

265
00:19:33,170 --> 00:19:34,922
The exact dates
aren't set yet, though.

266
00:19:36,424 --> 00:19:37,466
I guess...

267
00:19:38,509 --> 00:19:40,595
I won't see you for a while.

268
00:19:50,813 --> 00:19:52,231
Why don't you come with me?

269
00:19:54,317 --> 00:19:55,401
Pardon?

270
00:19:56,068 --> 00:19:58,404
They're providing
a car and a place for me there.

271
00:19:58,988 --> 00:20:01,991
You could study fashion
while I'm filming.

272
00:20:02,241 --> 00:20:03,492
Then we wouldn't have to be apart.

273
00:20:06,162 --> 00:20:07,371
What about the company?

274
00:20:08,289 --> 00:20:10,041
We can work that out.

275
00:20:10,708 --> 00:20:12,543
A lot of people
work remotely these days.

276
00:20:12,627 --> 00:20:15,338
Building experience there
could be better for you.

277
00:20:18,215 --> 00:20:19,342
You'd love it.

278
00:20:19,925 --> 00:20:23,262
LA is full
of fashion shows and brands.

279
00:20:28,934 --> 00:20:31,145
That does sound nice.

280
00:20:31,979 --> 00:20:33,022
In that sense

281
00:20:33,606 --> 00:20:35,066
I picked one for you too.

282
00:20:42,406 --> 00:20:45,493
I actually have
something for you too.

283
00:20:46,369 --> 00:20:47,495
What is it?

284
00:21:05,554 --> 00:21:06,681
A cardholder?

285
00:21:07,598 --> 00:21:11,352
Yes, I made it myself
at a leather workshop.

286
00:21:11,936 --> 00:21:13,229
This is really well-made.

287
00:21:13,854 --> 00:21:15,106
It's too precious to use.

288
00:21:17,942 --> 00:21:19,068
Thanks.

289
00:21:41,674 --> 00:21:42,758
LA...

290
00:21:54,854 --> 00:21:56,439
<i>Whatever choice you make</i>

291
00:21:56,522 --> 00:21:59,316
just make sure it's a choice
that's true to who you are.

292
00:22:16,459 --> 00:22:18,169
FASHION DIRECTOR NAM DA-REUM!

293
00:22:18,252 --> 00:22:20,421
APPELLO'S EMPLOYEE OF THE YEAR!

294
00:22:25,092 --> 00:22:26,927
UNFRAMED: KNOTTING
UNTYING TRADITIONS TO TIE IT ANEW

295
00:22:37,229 --> 00:22:39,231
APPELLO BRAND EXPANSION PROPOSAL

296
00:23:08,260 --> 00:23:09,595
<i>Exhale on your way up.</i>

297
00:23:11,013 --> 00:23:13,724
Inhale on your way down.

298
00:23:14,892 --> 00:23:16,727
Come up just a little higher.

299
00:23:18,979 --> 00:23:21,273
Hold it right here. One, two.

300
00:23:22,441 --> 00:23:23,484
All right.

301
00:23:23,776 --> 00:23:25,653
We're done for today.

302
00:23:27,238 --> 00:23:28,739
Please tidy up your space.

303
00:23:29,156 --> 00:23:30,157
Okay.

304
00:23:31,575 --> 00:23:34,495
- Great work.
- Thank you so much.

305
00:23:37,706 --> 00:23:38,707
Well...

306
00:23:42,545 --> 00:23:44,296
Mr. Min-woo, will you come

307
00:23:44,380 --> 00:23:46,048
to the last lesson
of the day next time?

308
00:23:49,844 --> 00:23:52,471
I'm pretty sure she gave me a sign.

309
00:23:54,974 --> 00:23:56,225
Was I wrong?

310
00:24:08,654 --> 00:24:11,240
Thank you for the last session today.

311
00:24:11,323 --> 00:24:14,451
- You too.
- Right.

312
00:24:14,535 --> 00:24:16,954
I'll get going, then. Goodbye.

313
00:24:17,580 --> 00:24:18,873
Really, I'm leaving.

314
00:24:21,125 --> 00:24:22,501
- Mr. Min-woo.
- Yes?

315
00:24:22,877 --> 00:24:24,336
We should head out together.

316
00:24:24,420 --> 00:24:27,506
Right? We're grabbing a bite, right?

317
00:24:27,840 --> 00:24:29,508
- Shall we?
- Let's go.

318
00:24:33,304 --> 00:24:34,889
{\an8}Wow, that looks so good.

319
00:24:35,890 --> 00:24:38,601
- You must be starving.
- Thank you.

320
00:24:38,851 --> 00:24:40,102
Today's session was tough, wasn't it?

321
00:24:40,185 --> 00:24:42,187
Not at all. It was a breeze.

322
00:24:43,022 --> 00:24:44,273
Thank you.

323
00:24:46,150 --> 00:24:48,110
You must be pretty extroverted

324
00:24:48,360 --> 00:24:50,029
to hit on someone
at a place like this.

325
00:24:50,279 --> 00:24:51,447
<i>How did you get here?</i>

326
00:24:51,530 --> 00:24:53,782
- I took a bus.
- Then on your way back

327
00:24:53,866 --> 00:24:55,451
you can take a chance on me.

328
00:24:56,911 --> 00:24:58,203
Oh, you remember that?

329
00:25:01,040 --> 00:25:02,333
That was a first for me.

330
00:25:02,499 --> 00:25:04,293
Seriously.

331
00:25:04,376 --> 00:25:07,171
I'm actually a total introvert.
I've never dated anyone.

332
00:25:07,588 --> 00:25:09,715
That day

333
00:25:10,382 --> 00:25:13,218
I fell for you and gathered
the courage for the first time ever.

334
00:25:15,471 --> 00:25:17,806
Is that your go-to pickup line?

335
00:25:17,890 --> 00:25:18,891
Yes.

336
00:25:19,308 --> 00:25:20,851
Just kidding.

337
00:25:21,435 --> 00:25:25,272
I tend to ramble a bit
when I'm around someone I like.

338
00:25:25,606 --> 00:25:27,942
- Why?
- To act like I'm not nervous.

339
00:25:30,235 --> 00:25:32,529
What about now, then?

340
00:25:32,613 --> 00:25:33,906
I'm completely like this.

341
00:25:40,162 --> 00:25:42,164
Did that make you laugh?
Guess that's a win.

342
00:25:43,791 --> 00:25:44,875
Anyway

343
00:25:44,959 --> 00:25:47,544
thank you so much for handling
that awful customer the other day.

344
00:25:47,628 --> 00:25:48,837
Don't mention it.

345
00:25:49,630 --> 00:25:52,841
How do you know
all the terms and conditions, though?

346
00:25:52,925 --> 00:25:54,468
No one actually reads those.

347
00:25:55,886 --> 00:25:57,054
It's a habit.

348
00:25:57,680 --> 00:26:00,265
The habit of wanting to win
the moment an argument breaks out.

349
00:26:00,724 --> 00:26:02,935
- It's your habit?
- It's just that

350
00:26:03,727 --> 00:26:04,895
reading text is part of my job.

351
00:26:08,941 --> 00:26:10,275
<i>Who is he, really?</i>

352
00:26:10,651 --> 00:26:11,944
<i>There's a surprising side to him.</i>

353
00:26:19,743 --> 00:26:21,578
BUCKET LIST FOR LA

354
00:26:23,372 --> 00:26:24,790
It's been updated.

355
00:26:25,749 --> 00:26:27,292
You've added an LA version too.

356
00:26:29,294 --> 00:26:32,297
You've always said making it
to Hollywood was your dream.

357
00:26:32,715 --> 00:26:33,716
Right.

358
00:26:34,216 --> 00:26:36,427
So naturally,
I spent a lot of time picturing it.

359
00:26:37,261 --> 00:26:40,180
We can cross these off together.

360
00:26:44,351 --> 00:26:46,895
We'll enjoy the night view
at the observatory

361
00:26:47,604 --> 00:26:49,231
and walk along the beach together.

362
00:26:50,149 --> 00:26:51,316
It's a perfect date itinerary.

363
00:27:00,993 --> 00:27:02,161
Chan.

364
00:27:02,870 --> 00:27:04,371
I have something to say.

365
00:27:06,123 --> 00:27:07,207
Something to say?

366
00:27:09,418 --> 00:27:10,419
You see

367
00:27:11,670 --> 00:27:13,255
I really enjoyed

368
00:27:14,631 --> 00:27:17,384
our time together,
and I definitely had butterflies.

369
00:27:20,471 --> 00:27:21,513
But then...

370
00:27:23,807 --> 00:27:25,100
I don't think

371
00:27:26,226 --> 00:27:27,561
I was being honest.

372
00:27:31,899 --> 00:27:32,941
What do you mean?

373
00:27:33,776 --> 00:27:35,110
With you

374
00:27:36,070 --> 00:27:37,112
and

375
00:27:38,614 --> 00:27:40,074
with myself.

376
00:27:42,159 --> 00:27:43,368
So today

377
00:27:44,036 --> 00:27:45,662
I'm going to stop pretending I'm okay

378
00:27:46,663 --> 00:27:48,332
and just be honest.

379
00:27:59,093 --> 00:28:01,095
I thought if I were with someone I like

380
00:28:01,929 --> 00:28:03,263
I'd be able to share

381
00:28:04,139 --> 00:28:05,182
my feelings with him

382
00:28:05,766 --> 00:28:08,936
by laughing, crying

383
00:28:10,437 --> 00:28:12,898
whining, and even fighting.

384
00:28:14,608 --> 00:28:17,736
But for some reason...

385
00:28:21,949 --> 00:28:23,158
I couldn't easily do that

386
00:28:24,785 --> 00:28:26,453
with you.

387
00:28:31,917 --> 00:28:33,168
I think

388
00:28:34,461 --> 00:28:35,629
I still see you

389
00:28:36,255 --> 00:28:37,381
more as an idol

390
00:28:38,215 --> 00:28:39,341
rather than

391
00:28:40,467 --> 00:28:41,927
a romantic partner.

392
00:28:46,014 --> 00:28:48,433
I still root for your dreams.

393
00:28:49,476 --> 00:28:51,270
But I have my own dreams
to chase now.

394
00:28:52,437 --> 00:28:54,815
The US sounds great

395
00:28:55,607 --> 00:28:56,775
but I love Appello.

396
00:28:59,903 --> 00:29:01,071
I love

397
00:29:02,239 --> 00:29:03,240
the work I do here.

398
00:29:05,033 --> 00:29:06,034
So I'd rather just

399
00:29:07,369 --> 00:29:09,496
stay as Nam Da-reum,
an employee of Appello...

400
00:29:13,834 --> 00:29:15,043
and remain...

401
00:29:19,548 --> 00:29:20,674
your fan.

402
00:29:48,660 --> 00:29:49,912
CHRYSANTHEMUM KNOT
<i>DONGSIMGYEOL </i>KNOT

403
00:29:57,252 --> 00:29:58,795
Here we go.
Nam Da-reum mode activated.

404
00:29:59,338 --> 00:30:01,256
Nam Da-reum mode?
What does that mean?

405
00:30:01,340 --> 00:30:03,258
Remember when we made
the challenge video?

406
00:30:03,342 --> 00:30:05,469
She worked even harder
when she was told to back off.

407
00:30:05,552 --> 00:30:08,889
She thrives when pushed to the brink.
I call it Nam Da-reum mode.

408
00:30:09,514 --> 00:30:13,894
Ms. Da-reum, you aren't being pushed
to the edge again, are you?

409
00:30:13,977 --> 00:30:16,146
Not at all. I just like doing it

410
00:30:16,897 --> 00:30:18,815
because it keeps
my mind from wandering.

411
00:30:23,904 --> 00:30:26,281
What happened to your hand?
Did you injure yourself?

412
00:30:27,366 --> 00:30:29,368
I'm currently fostering a kitten.

413
00:30:30,160 --> 00:30:34,373
I need to find someone to adopt it
but I've been too busy to even try.

414
00:30:34,456 --> 00:30:37,501
A cat? I've actually been
preparing to adopt one.

415
00:30:37,584 --> 00:30:39,336
Hold on. Can I see a picture?

416
00:30:39,419 --> 00:30:40,545
- Really?
- Yes.

417
00:30:40,629 --> 00:30:41,797
Just a second.

418
00:30:42,214 --> 00:30:45,550
- Do you like animals?
- Yes, totally.

419
00:30:46,426 --> 00:30:47,678
Me too.

420
00:30:48,345 --> 00:30:49,513
Isn't it adorable?

421
00:30:51,473 --> 00:30:52,599
The name is Jjak.

422
00:30:52,683 --> 00:30:53,976
There are actually two.

423
00:30:54,059 --> 00:30:56,395
Their names are Kung and Jjak,
like a matching beat.

424
00:30:56,478 --> 00:30:58,939
Oh, my gosh. It's adorable.

425
00:30:59,022 --> 00:31:01,316
No joke, I've wanted an orange tabby.

426
00:31:01,400 --> 00:31:02,943
- Are you serious?
- Dead serious.

427
00:31:03,568 --> 00:31:04,861
Here's another one.

428
00:31:05,988 --> 00:31:08,865
- Adorable, right?
- Oh, my. It's so cute.

429
00:31:17,874 --> 00:31:19,501
This is the script
from Director Park Chan-dong.

430
00:31:19,584 --> 00:31:22,587
Chan, your casting is finalized!

431
00:31:25,424 --> 00:31:27,217
THE TARGET: THE LAST AIM

432
00:31:29,469 --> 00:31:32,097
- What is it? You can't believe it?
- What?

433
00:31:32,472 --> 00:31:33,932
No, it's just that
things are going so well.

434
00:31:35,309 --> 00:31:36,810
Is that really your concern?

435
00:31:36,893 --> 00:31:38,812
Wait, all right.
Let's celebrate later.

436
00:31:38,895 --> 00:31:41,148
Since it's all shot in the States,
we've got tons to do.

437
00:31:41,231 --> 00:31:44,609
Clearing schedules, sorting visas,
getting you in shape...

438
00:31:44,693 --> 00:31:46,528
And if you need anything,
just write it down.

439
00:31:46,611 --> 00:31:48,572
Won-bin,
I can't let it end like this.

440
00:31:50,324 --> 00:31:52,034
Chan, where are you going?

441
00:32:12,179 --> 00:32:13,221
Mr. Kang.

442
00:32:16,767 --> 00:32:18,101
You're still here?

443
00:32:19,519 --> 00:32:20,937
I'm going to finish a bit more.

444
00:32:31,907 --> 00:32:34,159
You really don't have to...

445
00:32:37,037 --> 00:32:38,288
Thank you.

446
00:32:43,502 --> 00:32:46,171
No date tonight?

447
00:32:46,797 --> 00:32:47,798
No.

448
00:32:48,632 --> 00:32:51,802
I'm way
too swamped for that right now.

449
00:32:52,052 --> 00:32:53,428
Why are you doing
all this by yourself?

450
00:32:53,678 --> 00:32:54,971
I never gave such an order.

451
00:32:56,723 --> 00:32:58,308
My coworkers helped out a lot
during the day.

452
00:32:58,558 --> 00:33:01,645
I'm just finishing up what's left.

453
00:33:02,396 --> 00:33:03,730
It must be hard
taking on a major event

454
00:33:04,815 --> 00:33:05,857
all of a sudden.

455
00:33:07,901 --> 00:33:10,612
It's a little overwhelming.

456
00:33:11,071 --> 00:33:15,158
Still, it feels rewarding
to be in charge of something.

457
00:33:26,378 --> 00:33:27,879
You'll learn a lot

458
00:33:29,172 --> 00:33:30,340
from each project you handle.

459
00:33:31,466 --> 00:33:32,467
Right.

460
00:33:33,468 --> 00:33:34,469
Oh, right.

461
00:33:34,553 --> 00:33:37,556
Young-woo said
he wanted to adopt Kung and Jjak.

462
00:33:38,181 --> 00:33:41,476
You're sending them away already?

463
00:33:41,893 --> 00:33:43,770
I'm upset about it a bit too

464
00:33:43,854 --> 00:33:46,398
but it's great for Kung and Jjak.

465
00:33:47,190 --> 00:33:48,358
It is.

466
00:33:49,860 --> 00:33:52,863
I bought Kung lots of toys.

467
00:33:53,363 --> 00:33:54,656
What else did you get?

468
00:33:54,739 --> 00:33:56,616
I said you didn't have to.

469
00:33:57,742 --> 00:33:58,743
Still.

470
00:34:00,120 --> 00:34:01,121
Where did you get them?

471
00:34:01,788 --> 00:34:03,874
From stores and stuff.

472
00:34:10,672 --> 00:34:13,467
<i>Ms. Da-reum?
She's working late today.</i>

473
00:35:10,357 --> 00:35:11,525
Mr. Kang.

474
00:35:11,942 --> 00:35:14,736
Do you remember
what you said to me last time?

475
00:35:16,279 --> 00:35:17,280
What did I say?

476
00:35:18,907 --> 00:35:20,450
That whatever choice I make

477
00:35:20,534 --> 00:35:22,577
I should make sure
I'd be true to who I am.

478
00:35:28,792 --> 00:35:30,085
Thanks to what you said

479
00:35:31,127 --> 00:35:32,379
I could pluck up the courage.

480
00:35:41,930 --> 00:35:43,098
For the first time ever

481
00:35:44,849 --> 00:35:46,184
I was able to be honest.

482
00:35:47,769 --> 00:35:49,521
And I made a choice
that was true to myself.

483
00:35:53,483 --> 00:35:54,943
Thank you, Mr. Kang.

484
00:35:59,990 --> 00:36:02,784
You were just someone
who was always capable

485
00:36:04,536 --> 00:36:05,829
of making that choice.

486
00:36:12,502 --> 00:36:15,797
It seems more like it
now that you put it into words.

487
00:36:20,802 --> 00:36:23,722
<i>She broke it off with that guy, then.</i>

488
00:36:34,983 --> 00:36:37,360
- Ms. Da-reum.
- Yes?

489
00:36:39,487 --> 00:36:40,739
I have something to...

490
00:36:41,239 --> 00:36:42,741
I see you're hard at work.

491
00:36:45,243 --> 00:36:46,244
Why are you here?

492
00:36:46,870 --> 00:36:49,289
I heard you stayed behind
to prepare for the pop-up.

493
00:36:51,124 --> 00:36:52,125
Is this the DIY kit?

494
00:36:53,418 --> 00:36:54,544
Yes, Director.

495
00:37:00,967 --> 00:37:02,802
How is it made? Teach me.

496
00:37:05,263 --> 00:37:06,264
Take a seat.

497
00:37:21,363 --> 00:37:24,491
You work so fast, Director.

498
00:37:24,574 --> 00:37:27,452
I once signed
over 1,000 albums in a day.

499
00:37:27,952 --> 00:37:29,037
This is nothing.

500
00:37:29,663 --> 00:37:30,872
Fold it properly.

501
00:37:31,414 --> 00:37:33,166
Focus on the detail,
not just the speed.

502
00:37:34,292 --> 00:37:35,627
Yes, boss.

503
00:37:40,924 --> 00:37:42,133
Ms. Da-reum. Check this.

504
00:37:49,974 --> 00:37:52,519
So, Ms. Da-reum.

505
00:37:53,019 --> 00:37:55,855
Who are you a better match with
between us two?

506
00:37:57,857 --> 00:37:58,900
Sorry?

507
00:37:59,693 --> 00:38:00,819
Why do you want to know that?

508
00:38:02,112 --> 00:38:03,947
Everyone has a type.

509
00:38:15,792 --> 00:38:18,461
I'm still new, so I can't say.

510
00:38:18,837 --> 00:38:21,631
And you two are so different.

511
00:38:26,052 --> 00:38:28,847
What a safe, political reply.

512
00:38:34,185 --> 00:38:37,856
I just wanted to know
if you were leaning toward anyone.

513
00:39:30,992 --> 00:39:32,035
We need to talk.

514
00:39:36,537 --> 00:39:37,622
Did you really

515
00:39:38,456 --> 00:39:39,916
come here today about work?

516
00:39:40,958 --> 00:39:42,001
Why?

517
00:39:42,585 --> 00:39:44,170
And when you came
to Master Im's place?

518
00:39:48,591 --> 00:39:50,343
Because this is an important project.

519
00:39:52,053 --> 00:39:53,054
Do you

520
00:39:55,098 --> 00:39:56,307
like Ms. Da-reum?

521
00:40:04,107 --> 00:40:05,149
I do like her.

522
00:40:10,279 --> 00:40:11,447
She's my favorite employee.

523
00:40:13,282 --> 00:40:15,618
Who wouldn't like someone
who works so hard?

524
00:40:16,077 --> 00:40:17,120
Only as an employee?

525
00:40:18,621 --> 00:40:19,956
What do you want me to say?

526
00:40:21,040 --> 00:40:22,959
You tried to go after her just now.

527
00:40:27,296 --> 00:40:28,464
What about you, then?

528
00:40:29,757 --> 00:40:31,676
Are you protecting your employee

529
00:40:32,218 --> 00:40:33,302
or are you keeping me in check?

530
00:40:39,934 --> 00:40:40,977
You won't answer either.

531
00:40:45,648 --> 00:40:47,191
Once you decide to become honest

532
00:40:51,028 --> 00:40:52,363
so will I.

533
00:41:18,848 --> 00:41:19,932
<i>Ms. Da-reum.</i>

534
00:41:20,933 --> 00:41:23,394
Who are you a better match with
between us two?

535
00:41:26,522 --> 00:41:28,983
<i>I want to start dating you.</i>

536
00:41:29,525 --> 00:41:30,526
<i>Da-reum.</i>

537
00:41:31,235 --> 00:41:33,321
<i>I'm sorry for that day.</i>

538
00:41:33,613 --> 00:41:35,782
<i>Please don't mind me.</i>

539
00:41:36,324 --> 00:41:38,242
<i>I feel bad
to send you home like this.</i>

540
00:41:38,326 --> 00:41:40,077
<i>I'm really fine.</i>

541
00:41:40,787 --> 00:41:42,205
<i>But you're not okay.</i>

542
00:41:42,747 --> 00:41:45,750
<i>At least, in front of me
you can say it's not okay.</i>

543
00:41:53,341 --> 00:41:54,342
<i>I just wanted to know</i>

544
00:41:54,675 --> 00:41:56,636
<i>if you were leaning toward anyone.</i>

545
00:42:03,142 --> 00:42:04,727
<i>Coming!</i>

546
00:42:05,019 --> 00:42:06,437
Hi, thank you.

547
00:42:06,521 --> 00:42:08,231
Enjoy the food and have a happy day.

548
00:42:11,025 --> 00:42:12,735
<i>Have a happy day.</i>

549
00:42:13,778 --> 00:42:16,197
<i>I hope my voice brings you
a small piece of happiness</i>

550
00:42:16,280 --> 00:42:17,990
<i>every single day.</i>

551
00:42:18,741 --> 00:42:20,868
<i>This is Roy from D.N.X signing off.</i>

552
00:42:35,842 --> 00:42:38,094
That was most definitely Roy's voice.

553
00:42:57,738 --> 00:42:59,490
I wanted to have <i>kalguksu </i>today.

554
00:42:59,782 --> 00:43:01,284
We failed yet again today.

555
00:43:01,367 --> 00:43:03,619
When will we ever get to eat there?

556
00:43:03,703 --> 00:43:06,205
We don't stand a chance
unless we take the morning off

557
00:43:06,289 --> 00:43:07,373
to wait in line.

558
00:43:08,291 --> 00:43:10,334
I really wanted to try out
<i>Kalguksu Jip.</i>

559
00:43:10,418 --> 00:43:11,794
Me too.

560
00:43:11,878 --> 00:43:14,505
Shall we go to the rooftop
for a stroll to digest our lunch?

561
00:43:14,589 --> 00:43:15,840
- Good idea.
- Isn't it?

562
00:43:15,923 --> 00:43:17,592
I have some work to get back to.

563
00:43:18,009 --> 00:43:19,927
Ms. Min-a, shall we go, then?

564
00:43:20,261 --> 00:43:21,304
Yes, sure.

565
00:43:21,387 --> 00:43:22,471
- See you later.
- Bye.

566
00:43:22,847 --> 00:43:24,307
See you in a bit.

567
00:43:29,604 --> 00:43:31,480
You didn't go out to lunch, Ms. Seo?

568
00:43:31,564 --> 00:43:32,815
I'm leaving now.

569
00:43:33,441 --> 00:43:34,817
I see you had an early lunch.

570
00:43:34,901 --> 00:43:36,736
- Yes. Enjoy your meal.
- Thanks.

571
00:43:57,214 --> 00:43:59,175
Did the cleaning lady come by?

572
00:44:11,270 --> 00:44:13,648
It looks like you're running away.

573
00:44:13,731 --> 00:44:15,608
Why's there so much stuff for a cat?

574
00:44:15,691 --> 00:44:17,318
I kept buying stuff.

575
00:44:21,822 --> 00:44:25,326
Here, hand over the cat

576
00:44:26,327 --> 00:44:27,787
and tell her how you feel.

577
00:44:30,039 --> 00:44:31,290
What are you on about?

578
00:44:31,374 --> 00:44:33,960
Don't miss out
on an opportunity like this.

579
00:44:34,043 --> 00:44:36,087
- Good luck over there.
- What the heck?

580
00:44:36,629 --> 00:44:37,672
Go on home.

581
00:44:39,674 --> 00:44:42,301
Good luck, okay? Do your thing.

582
00:44:44,553 --> 00:44:45,596
I'm leaving.

583
00:44:50,476 --> 00:44:51,727
How I feel?

584
00:44:52,728 --> 00:44:54,021
<i>Tell her how you feel.</i>

585
00:44:56,691 --> 00:44:58,484
<i>Someone close by.</i>

586
00:45:15,876 --> 00:45:16,919
Hang on.

587
00:45:19,922 --> 00:45:21,966
<i>I'll come by around 8 p.m.</i>

588
00:45:22,466 --> 00:45:25,261
<i>Great. Kung and Jjak
will meet at last.</i>

589
00:45:26,178 --> 00:45:28,889
<i>There's a lot of stuff,
so I'll come to your place.</i>

590
00:45:29,265 --> 00:45:30,516
<i>I'm setting off now.</i>

591
00:45:31,726 --> 00:45:33,310
He's so considerate.

592
00:45:42,945 --> 00:45:44,113
<i>See you again, Da-reum.</i>

593
00:45:48,826 --> 00:45:50,077
If Mr. Kang sees this...

594
00:45:50,870 --> 00:45:51,912
No!

595
00:46:08,596 --> 00:46:09,597
Am I done?

596
00:46:29,241 --> 00:46:30,576
<i>Tell her how you feel.</i>

597
00:46:35,706 --> 00:46:37,833
Hello, Kung.

598
00:46:41,504 --> 00:46:43,005
Wait here.

599
00:46:44,048 --> 00:46:46,383
That must've been heavy.
Thank you, Mr. Kang.

600
00:46:51,388 --> 00:46:52,473
Wear these.

601
00:46:54,600 --> 00:46:57,269
- The thing is...
- Yes?

602
00:46:59,438 --> 00:47:01,398
It's my first time
visiting a lady's home.

603
00:47:03,109 --> 00:47:05,361
I hope you don't mind the intrusion.

604
00:47:05,444 --> 00:47:07,696
It's fine. Make yourself at home.

605
00:47:16,622 --> 00:47:18,165
You can take your time.

606
00:47:35,850 --> 00:47:37,101
Have some tea.

607
00:47:38,602 --> 00:47:39,687
Thanks.

608
00:47:52,032 --> 00:47:53,409
Jjak.

609
00:47:54,160 --> 00:47:58,455
Listen. Kung is here to see you.

610
00:47:58,539 --> 00:48:00,291
They've grown a lot.

611
00:48:00,374 --> 00:48:03,002
You think so?
Isn't Kung the same size?

612
00:48:03,919 --> 00:48:04,920
Kung is...

613
00:48:07,464 --> 00:48:08,632
Where's Kung?

614
00:48:10,593 --> 00:48:11,677
Kung.

615
00:48:15,681 --> 00:48:17,016
When did it get in there?

616
00:48:19,101 --> 00:48:20,186
I'll go get Kung.

617
00:48:21,562 --> 00:48:24,356
- Kung.
- What?

618
00:48:25,983 --> 00:48:27,985
You wait here. Oh, no.

619
00:48:28,235 --> 00:48:29,403
Kung?

620
00:48:33,115 --> 00:48:34,491
- Wait!
- Scared me.

621
00:48:35,492 --> 00:48:37,828
You can't go in there. Not ever.

622
00:48:37,912 --> 00:48:38,913
It's my secret...

623
00:48:41,457 --> 00:48:43,000
It's my underwear closet.

624
00:48:44,960 --> 00:48:46,086
I apologize.

625
00:48:46,503 --> 00:48:47,504
Then...

626
00:48:49,006 --> 00:48:51,133
I won't even take a peek.

627
00:48:58,432 --> 00:49:00,017
Sit over there and wait.

628
00:49:00,100 --> 00:49:03,187
- I'll get Kung and join you.
- Okay.

629
00:49:03,812 --> 00:49:07,233
- I don't see a thing right now.
- Good.

630
00:49:12,112 --> 00:49:15,616
SHINING BRIGHT, LEE CHAN

631
00:49:15,699 --> 00:49:17,409
That was
the biggest crisis of my life.

632
00:49:23,207 --> 00:49:26,794
I can't hide that I'm Chan's fan
from Mr. Kang forever.

633
00:49:27,962 --> 00:49:28,963
Should I just

634
00:49:29,713 --> 00:49:31,715
tell him the truth?

635
00:49:37,012 --> 00:49:38,305
They really recognize each other.

636
00:49:39,139 --> 00:49:40,599
Isn't that fascinating?

637
00:49:40,766 --> 00:49:43,060
You said they fought
and ate each other's food

638
00:49:43,143 --> 00:49:44,395
when they were together.

639
00:49:46,730 --> 00:49:50,359
They fight when they're together
and miss each other when apart.

640
00:49:52,569 --> 00:49:53,821
It must be like that

641
00:49:55,322 --> 00:49:56,365
for people...

642
00:49:59,660 --> 00:50:00,786
and for cats, too.

643
00:50:08,294 --> 00:50:10,504
<i>Yes. Now is the time.</i>

644
00:50:12,131 --> 00:50:13,966
Mr. Kang.

645
00:50:15,092 --> 00:50:18,554
The truth is...

646
00:50:19,763 --> 00:50:20,848
Yes?

647
00:50:22,474 --> 00:50:23,600
So...

648
00:50:25,102 --> 00:50:27,354
- For a long time...
- Excuse me.

649
00:50:30,524 --> 00:50:31,608
Yes, hello.

650
00:50:32,192 --> 00:50:35,279
I'm not at home.
I'll check when I get back.

651
00:50:38,115 --> 00:50:40,576
- What were you about to say?
- What?

652
00:50:44,621 --> 00:50:48,125
Oh, I was going to thank you
for bringing Kung.

653
00:50:50,127 --> 00:50:51,420
I should thank you.

654
00:50:52,087 --> 00:50:53,630
I did bring Kung over

655
00:50:54,381 --> 00:50:55,924
but I got to see Jjak again.

656
00:50:59,011 --> 00:51:00,637
And I got to see you again.

657
00:51:03,223 --> 00:51:04,308
It's nice.

658
00:51:23,535 --> 00:51:24,828
Look at the time.

659
00:51:25,871 --> 00:51:28,207
- I should go.
- That's so sudden.

660
00:51:29,375 --> 00:51:30,584
You should rest.

661
00:51:31,752 --> 00:51:33,879
Kung, I'm leaving.

662
00:51:35,506 --> 00:51:36,965
I'll see you at work, then.

663
00:51:37,049 --> 00:51:40,636
- Drive home safely, Mr. Kang.
- Bye.

664
00:51:53,524 --> 00:51:54,775
Did she get the message?

665
00:52:04,827 --> 00:52:06,286
<i>I got to see you again.</i>

666
00:52:07,246 --> 00:52:08,247
It's nice.

667
00:52:09,748 --> 00:52:11,500
"I got to see you again.

668
00:52:12,584 --> 00:52:13,836
It's nice."

669
00:52:17,673 --> 00:52:18,882
I agree.

670
00:52:30,668 --> 00:52:32,002
Yes, that's right.

671
00:52:32,670 --> 00:52:35,464
How did you get the company photos?

672
00:52:36,674 --> 00:52:39,593
Oh, really? No wonder.

673
00:52:40,469 --> 00:52:42,054
I look forward to your article.

674
00:52:47,726 --> 00:52:49,019
- Hello.
- Hello.

675
00:52:49,103 --> 00:52:50,980
- Hi. Sit over here, please.
- Hello.

676
00:52:54,233 --> 00:52:56,110
- I'll get everything ready.
- Okay.

677
00:53:01,991 --> 00:53:05,077
I heard you'll be working
with Director Park Chan-dong.

678
00:53:05,327 --> 00:53:08,247
- I'm really happy for you.
- Thanks.

679
00:53:10,624 --> 00:53:13,294
I'm working
on a global project of my own.

680
00:53:13,794 --> 00:53:14,837
We're filming in the US.

681
00:53:16,714 --> 00:53:18,382
- In the US?
- Yes.

682
00:53:19,091 --> 00:53:20,426
What interesting timing.

683
00:53:21,760 --> 00:53:25,097
It looks like
we're meant to keep crossing paths.

684
00:53:36,400 --> 00:53:37,901
They're so adorable.

685
00:53:37,985 --> 00:53:41,196
I couldn't sleep for days.
They're so cute.

686
00:53:42,114 --> 00:53:43,240
Oh, my gosh.

687
00:53:44,491 --> 00:53:45,743
- Hi.
- Hello.

688
00:53:51,206 --> 00:53:52,333
You're leaving together?

689
00:53:53,042 --> 00:53:56,045
Yes. He's coming by to get the cats.

690
00:53:56,420 --> 00:53:57,630
I'm on my way home, too.

691
00:53:58,130 --> 00:53:59,173
I'll tag along.

692
00:54:00,424 --> 00:54:01,675
I'll drive you there.

693
00:54:02,885 --> 00:54:05,763
- We're headed in the same direction.
- I'd like that.

694
00:54:42,299 --> 00:54:45,844
Kung and Jjak. Look after yourselves.

695
00:54:46,804 --> 00:54:48,806
Don't forget me, okay?

696
00:54:50,683 --> 00:54:53,560
- Bye.
- Take care.

697
00:54:57,022 --> 00:54:59,983
I'll take really good care
of Kung and Jjak.

698
00:55:00,067 --> 00:55:02,736
Mr. Kang. Thank you so much
for helping with the luggage.

699
00:55:04,405 --> 00:55:05,614
Bye, Young-woo.

700
00:55:06,031 --> 00:55:08,742
If you don't mind me asking,
do you think...

701
00:55:10,285 --> 00:55:11,578
Never mind.

702
00:55:14,248 --> 00:55:15,833
By any chance...

703
00:55:23,173 --> 00:55:25,843
Wouldn't it be a shame
to part like this?

704
00:55:25,926 --> 00:55:27,845
Since we're coworkers

705
00:55:27,928 --> 00:55:29,763
how about some coffee
with Mr. Kang too?

706
00:55:31,515 --> 00:55:32,683
That's a no.

707
00:55:33,183 --> 00:55:35,811
Cats get very stressed out
in unfamiliar settings.

708
00:55:35,894 --> 00:55:38,021
They need their owner
on their first day.

709
00:55:38,105 --> 00:55:40,482
Yes, right, of course.
You're the CEO for a reason.

710
00:55:40,566 --> 00:55:42,943
- Let's pass on it today.
- Yes. Maybe next time.

711
00:55:43,902 --> 00:55:45,988
Go on home
and help the cats settle in.

712
00:55:46,405 --> 00:55:48,240
I'll do that. Goodbye.

713
00:55:48,782 --> 00:55:49,783
Bye.

714
00:55:51,869 --> 00:55:52,870
Ms. Da-reum.

715
00:55:52,953 --> 00:55:54,788
Let's hang out soon.

716
00:55:55,080 --> 00:55:56,457
Without Mr. Kang.

717
00:55:58,083 --> 00:55:59,209
Sounds good.

718
00:56:04,006 --> 00:56:07,426
Kung, Jjak, live happily ever after.

719
00:56:08,635 --> 00:56:10,262
Look after each other.

720
00:56:14,433 --> 00:56:15,517
Don't fight.

721
00:56:23,066 --> 00:56:25,652
Ms. Da-reum. Are you crying?

722
00:56:27,905 --> 00:56:28,947
No.

723
00:56:30,699 --> 00:56:33,243
I guess I got attached to them.

724
00:56:38,540 --> 00:56:39,625
I think

725
00:56:41,043 --> 00:56:42,544
I got more attached.

726
00:56:47,090 --> 00:56:49,635
I liked asking each day
if they'd eaten.

727
00:56:51,762 --> 00:56:53,347
The weird photos too.

728
00:56:55,641 --> 00:56:56,934
I looked forward to them.

729
00:57:00,521 --> 00:57:01,522
Yes.

730
00:57:02,481 --> 00:57:03,690
Now the cats are gone.

731
00:57:07,820 --> 00:57:09,112
I have no reason to contact you.

732
00:57:15,744 --> 00:57:16,787
Well...

733
00:57:30,133 --> 00:57:31,510
What's wrong with me?

734
00:57:38,517 --> 00:57:39,685
Shall we have dinner together?

735
00:57:41,478 --> 00:57:42,771
It would be a shame
to part like this.

736
00:57:47,317 --> 00:57:49,027
Sure. I'd like that.

737
00:57:50,779 --> 00:57:51,822
- Let's go.
- Okay.

738
00:57:57,619 --> 00:57:59,329
Next. Come on in.

739
00:57:59,413 --> 00:58:02,916
I really wanted to try this place.
How did you hear about it?

740
00:58:04,251 --> 00:58:05,252
Well...

741
00:58:05,627 --> 00:58:06,628
KALGUKSU JIP

742
00:58:06,712 --> 00:58:09,131
- I heard they're famous.
- They are.

743
00:58:10,382 --> 00:58:12,509
We failed yet again today.

744
00:58:12,593 --> 00:58:14,636
When will we ever get to eat there?

745
00:58:16,013 --> 00:58:18,265
I really wanted to try out
Kalguksu Jip.

746
00:58:18,348 --> 00:58:20,309
- Me, too.
<i>- Kalguksu?</i>

747
00:58:20,392 --> 00:58:21,393
WHAT ARE YOU LOOKING FOR?

748
00:58:21,476 --> 00:58:24,980
Famous <i>kalguksu </i>places nearby.

749
00:58:27,858 --> 00:58:29,192
I found it.

750
00:58:35,115 --> 00:58:37,868
- You wanted to try this that much?
- Yes.

751
00:58:37,951 --> 00:58:40,370
They don't take reservations,
so it's really hard to get in.

752
00:58:42,372 --> 00:58:43,373
Over here.

753
00:58:47,920 --> 00:58:49,004
Sorry about that.

754
00:58:51,548 --> 00:58:52,549
Stand on this side.

755
00:58:53,675 --> 00:58:54,676
Thank you.

756
00:59:06,271 --> 00:59:08,315
Two bowls of <i>kalguksu.</i>

757
00:59:09,733 --> 00:59:11,902
- Thank you.
- Enjoy yourselves.

758
00:59:12,903 --> 00:59:14,613
Look at the color of the broth.

759
00:59:14,696 --> 00:59:16,573
There's no way this isn't good.

760
00:59:16,949 --> 00:59:18,659
Okay, just a moment, please.

761
00:59:19,910 --> 00:59:22,621
- More pickled radish, please.
- Leave that here.

762
00:59:26,667 --> 00:59:27,709
What is it?

763
00:59:28,794 --> 00:59:30,170
Do you not like it?

764
00:59:39,346 --> 00:59:41,473
This tastes amazing.

765
00:59:41,807 --> 00:59:44,393
Right? They're famous for a reason.

766
00:59:44,768 --> 00:59:46,103
Let's dig in.

767
00:59:56,571 --> 00:59:57,614
It's good.

768
01:00:01,159 --> 01:00:02,327
That was awesome.

769
01:00:02,869 --> 01:00:05,831
- It was worth the wait, wasn't it?
- Yes.

770
01:00:09,418 --> 01:00:11,461
Mr. Kang, look at that.

771
01:00:12,045 --> 01:00:13,171
STAR GAME ARCADE

772
01:00:13,255 --> 01:00:14,506
Doesn't that look like Jjak?

773
01:00:14,923 --> 01:00:19,052
That expression
and the light-lipped mouth.

774
01:00:19,136 --> 01:00:20,303
It's totally Jjak.

775
01:00:20,804 --> 01:00:21,847
How cute.

776
01:00:23,306 --> 01:00:24,683
- Do you want it?
- What?

777
01:00:26,935 --> 01:00:28,687
Mr. Kang.

778
01:00:30,105 --> 01:00:31,356
INSERT COIN HERE

779
01:00:51,793 --> 01:00:53,712
Yes, I got it.

780
01:01:02,596 --> 01:01:03,597
Darn it!

781
01:01:07,517 --> 01:01:09,644
Mr. Kang, that's enough.

782
01:01:09,728 --> 01:01:12,147
Watching you
was more than enough fun.

783
01:01:12,230 --> 01:01:15,275
- No, I see the pattern now.
- What?

784
01:01:17,194 --> 01:01:19,112
The claw's pressure is consistent

785
01:01:19,196 --> 01:01:21,740
but if you look carefully,
it's skewed slightly to the left.

786
01:01:21,990 --> 01:01:22,991
I failed just now

787
01:01:24,159 --> 01:01:25,368
because the angle was wrong.

788
01:01:28,080 --> 01:01:31,833
Mr. Kang. Why are you
so serious about this?

789
01:01:33,877 --> 01:01:35,045
We have a goal.

790
01:01:35,754 --> 01:01:36,755
We want Jjak.

791
01:01:37,672 --> 01:01:39,174
